-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",338,{
[10785]="7003A62F\n1\tCollect the Great Boar of Everholt's skull\tThe symbol of vengeance that has driven the Boar-tribe Orcs hangs from a crudely put together totem. You should take the skull and bring it to Cútha in Beaconwatch.\n2\tCollect the Great Boar of Everholt's skull\tThe symbol of vengeance that has driven the Boar-tribe Orcs hangs from a crudely put together totem. You should take the skull and bring it to Cútha in Beaconwatch.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have taken the Boar of Everholt's skull from the Boar-tribe.\n",
[10786]="70061BC3\n1\tGather samples of river water (total: 3)\tMurig needs samples of water from different points along the river. Collect water from the river-bank.\n2\tTalk to Murig\tMurig is near the river-bank, down the hill from Bloodhollow. Talk to Murig.\n3\tTest the water sample from Bloodhollow\030Test the water sample taken a moderate distance from Bloodhollow\030Test the water sample taken farthest from Bloodhollow\tMurig has arranged three basins of water. Test which basin has the cleanest water by using each of the three basins.\n4\tTalk to Murig\tYou have tested all the water samples. Talk to Murig.\n",
[10787]="70058CF9\n1\tAid Glóin with 'Beyond the High-threshold'\030Aid Glóin with 'After the Fall'\030Aid Glóin with 'At the Gates'\tGlóin can be found in the keep of Annâk-khurfu. Glóin has asked you to aid him and his scouts in securing the approach to Mount Gundabad.\n2\tTalk to Glóin at Annâk-khurfu\tGlóin can be found in the keep of Annâk-khurfu. Glóin has asked you to aid him and his scouts in securing the approach to Mount Gundabad.\n",
[10788]="70036C7A\n1\tSeal the culvert opening with rocks ([see journal]/18)\tThe Orcs have blasted a hole into the culvert upon the wall and are infiltrating through the gap. Assist the Rohirrim workers as they attempt to seal the opening to prevent further enemies from getting through the defences. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[10789]="700381C1\n1\tSeal the culvert opening with rocks ([see journal]/18)\tThe Orcs have blasted a hole into the culvert upon the wall and are infiltrating through the gap. Assist the Rohirrim labourers as they attempt to seal the opening to prevent further enemies from getting through the defences. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[10790]="7000EB73\n1\tScout the Grimwood Lumber-camp\tThe Grimwood Lumber-camp lies to the south of Gramsfoot. Soldier Búzog ordered you to reinforce the Grimwood Lumber-camp.\n2\tTalk to Soldier Búzog\tSoldier Búzog is at Gramsfoot. You should report to Soldier Búzog.\n",
[10791]="7001487B\n1\tFind the ancient tome\tThe library called Katûb-zahar indicated by the journal is located north of Gazatmur, north-east of the Dolven-view. You should search the ancient libraries of Khazad-dûm for the ancient tome.\n2\tBring the ancient tome to Sót in the Dolven-view\tSót is at the Dolven-view, south-west of Katûb-zahar. You should bring the tome you found to Sót. He will be eager to peruse it.\n",
[10792]="7006BF46\n1\tDefeat brigands in Zikrum-dûl (total: 8)\tDilûsu has asked you to help him deal with a group of brigands near Zikrum-dûl who have been attacking people as they flee the Orcs.\n2\tReturn to Dilûsu near Zikrum-dûl\tReturn to Dilûsu now that you have made the area safer from the brigands.\n",
[10793]="7003FFDC\n1\tRecover books (total: 4)\tThe books must be saved and preserved.\n",
[10794]="7003FF7C\n1\tRecover piles of gold (total: 6)\tPiles of gold have fallen out of the crates and should be recovered.\n",
[10795]="70039B5F\n1\tTalk to Thane Edric\tThane Edric can be found outside the Mead Hall of Entwade in eastern Kingstead. Éowyn has asked you to travel to Entwade to assist Thane Edric in securing the Wade as his people evacuate to a more defensible shelter.\n",
[10796]="7003FFF6\n1\tDisable traps (total: 8)\tThe traps must be removed for the people of Dol Amroth to be safe.\n",
[10797]="70015E2F\n1\tCollect seeds (total: 8)\tHolly-seeds can be found on the bushes growing underneath the trees in Glâd Ereg, south of Gwingris. Celebrandir has asked you to collect holly-seeds for him, so that he may begin replanting the wood.\n2\tBring the seeds to Celebrandir at Gwingris\tCelebrandir is at Gwingris, north of Glâd Ereg. Celebrandir is awaiting the seeds you collected.\n",
[10798]="70071B47\n1\tTBD Return to quest giver\tTBD Return to Quest Bestower\n",
[10799]="7002844B\n1\tCollect seedlings (total: 8)\tSeedlings can be found throughout the Vale of Nan Curunír. Dagoras asked you to gather up the seedlings struggling to survive in the Vale of Nan Curunír.\n2\tBring the seedlings to Dagoras' ally\tThe ally Dagoras mentioned might be up the ridge to the north-east from Dagoras' camp. Dagoras asked you to bring the seedlings to Dagoras' mysterious ally.\n",
[10800]="70018F4C\n1\tReturn the preserved seeds to Gailthin\tThe copse of trees Gailthin speaks of lay a short distance from her. Gailthin asked you to search the patches of leaves for any sign of preserved seed that might be used to restore the grove to its former beauty.\n",
[10801]="7006BF49\n1\tInvestigate the outskirts of Kûr Anzar for signs of Razâl\tRazâl, Mizâdi's trusted scout, hasn't reported back in a day. Investigate the eastern outskirts of Kûr Anzar for signs of Razâl. Kûr Anzar is located east of Urmâkh.\n2\tFree Razâl from his bonds so you both can escape\tFree Razâl from his bonds so you both can escape before the Barkhûshim notice you.\n3\tScout the first outlook into Kûr Anzar\030Scout the second outlook into Kûr Anzar\030Scout the third outlook into Kûr Anzar\tFind the three locations Razâl mentioned on the western outskirts north of where he was captured and scout Kûr Anzar from each of them.\n4\tSpeak with Mizâdi in Urmâkh\tSpeak with Mizâdi in Urmâkh.\n",
[10802]="7007251A\n1\tSpeak with Rhadrog at Zajâna\tViznak directs you to return to Rhadrog and Faeron in Zajâna, convinced that the Blight Lady they pursue has arrived here in Adagím.\n2\tSpeak with Faeron near the fountain in Zajâna\tAfter speaking with Rhadrog, he is resolved to seeking out Lhaereth and asks that you inform Faeron at the fountain in Zajâna.\n",
[10803]="70022418\n1\tFind the Library of Tham Mírdain\tThe Library of Tham Mírdain can be found in Mirobel, in the south-west region of Eregion. Ornras of Echad Mirobel has asked you to find the entrance to an ancient library.\n",
[10804]="70055007\n1\tTalk to Javatar\tBy completing this quest, you will be marked as completing Seeker of Knowledge\n",
[10805]="70009989\n1\tCollect rotted limbs (total: 6)\tThe Twisted Grove lies south-west of the Eavespires. Lithuifin has asked you to seek evidence of the power which has corrupted the Twisted Grove. He asked you to collect rotted limbs and bring them to him.\n2\tBring the rotted limbs to Lithuifin\tLithuifin is at the Eavespires, on the north-west shore of Lake Evendim. You should bring the rotted limbs you have collected to Lithuifin.\n",
[10806]="7004962B\n1\tDestroy vents (total: 6)\tVents can be found in Nargroth. You should destroy vents to attract Dúrossul's attention.\n2\tDestroy a more prominent vent and defeat Dúrossul\tVents can be found in Nargroth. You should destroy vents to attract Dúrossul's attention.\n3\tReturn to the Watching Stone\tThe Watching Stone can be found in Nargroth. You should return to the Watching Stone.\n",
[10807]="7000B2BB\n1\tTalk to Tórth\tTórth can be found outside the Blue Stone Garrison near the waterfall in Thorin's Hall. Guard-captain Unnarr has asked that you speak with Tórth to aid in the fight against the Dourhands.\n",
[10808]="700453E4\n1\tCollect Warg hides in Taur Drúadan (total: 10)\tWarg hides can be found from defeating Wargs in Taur Drúadan. You should defeat Wargs to collect their hides.\n2\tBring the Warg hides to Gnô-buri-Krûg\tGnô-buri-Krûg can be found in Drû Bhûta. You should bring the Warg hides to Gnô-buri-Krûg.\n",
[10809]="7006C587\n1\tTalk to Tharashil\tAmalíbi asks you to make your way south of Ghalbûru to a hidden oasis called Shonith, where Elves live and seclude themselves from the difficulties and trials of Man.\n",
[10810]="7004961A\n1\tDestroy pillars (total: 6)\tPillars can be found in Nargroth. You should destroy pillars to attract Nargúr's attention.\n2\tDestroy a more prominent pillar and defeat Nargúr\tPillars can be found in Nargroth. You should destroy pillars to attract Nargúr's attention.\n3\tReturn to the Watching Stone\tThe Watching Stone can be found in Nargroth. You should return to the Watching Stone.\n",
[10811]="70049629\n1\tDestroy statues (total: 6)\tStatues can be found in Nargroth. You should destroy statues to attract Narthalum's attention.\n2\tDestroy a more prominent statue and defeat Narthalum\tStatues can be found in Nargroth. You should destroy statues to attract Narthalum's attention.\n3\tReturn to the Watching Stone\tThe Watching Stone can be found in Nargroth. You should return to the Watching-stone.\n",
[10812]="70000D95\n1\tTalk to Cam Puddifoot\tCam Puddifoot is at his home in the middle of Budgeford. The first ingredient Hyacinth Took has sent you after is saltpetre. She suggested you visit her friend Cam Puddifoot, a pig-farmer in Budgeford.\n",
[10813]="7001CCD9\n1\tFind signs of the Malledhrim's passing at the Gostannon (total: 7)\tThe road to the Gostannon lies to the north of Amon Angeled, leading eastwards. Dannaswen has asked you to patrol the road to the Gostannon in order to determine the strength of the Enemy there.\n2\tBring the Malledhrim weapons to Dannaswen atop Amon Angened\tDannaswen is at the Elf-waypost atop Amon Angened, south of the Gostannon. You should bring the Malledhrim weapons you found back to Dannaswen and explain where you discovered them.\n",
[10814]="70066065\n1\tCollect cut wood (total: 10)\tRusgwen has asked you to gather cut wood from the tree dotted areas around Calembel.\n2\tReturn to Rusgwen\tYou should bring the cut wood you gathered back to Rusgwen in Calembel.\n",
[10815]="700563D7\n1\tComplete 'The Treasure Bugan'\tTheodore Gorse is searching for his stolen treasures.\n2\tComplete 'The Treasure Bugan' (total: 3)\tTheodore Gorse is searching for his stolen treasures. NOTE: Treasure Bugans can be found in many of the Scaling Instances.\n3\tTalk to Theodore Gorse in Bree, Rivendell, or Twenty-first Hall\tTheodore Gorse is searching for his stolen treasures and can be found in Bree, Rivendell, and the Twenty-first Hall. You should talk to Theodore Gorse.\n",
[10816]="70027280\n1\tDig in the disturbed earth at the foot of the Tree of Tribute\tThe earth is disturbed at the foot of the Tree of Tribute, south-west of the Rohirrim scout-camp. Saeradan told you to follow the clues to the source of the evil in the Gravenwood. You should dig in the disturbed earth.\n",
})
